_tafe_building%2C_geelong.jpg","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Marcus Wong Wongm","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gordon_institute_of_tafe_building,_geelong.jpg"}},{"id":"geelong_buckley_falls","areaId":"geelong","name":"Buckley Falls","category":"park","tags":["nature","hiking"],"location":{"lat":-38.15083,"lng":144.30694},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"geelong_buckley_falls","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":114,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-23"},"hashtags":["buckleyfalls","geelong"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Buckley Falls is a waterfall consisting of a series of rapids on the Barwon River in Geelong, Victoria, Australia, located between the suburbs of Highton and Fyansford. The falls form part of a popular riverside reserve featuring walking trails, lookouts and historical sites.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Buckley Falls","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Buckley_Falls%2C_evening_%288_June_19%29.jpg/1280px-Buckley_Falls%2C_evening_%288_June_19%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Buckley_Falls%2C_evening_%288_June_19%29.jpg/500px-Buckley_Falls%2C_evening_%288_June_19%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":777,"author":"Thom Devereux","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buckley_Falls,_evening_(8_June_19).jpg"}},{"id":"geelong_national_wool_museum","areaId":"geelong","name":"National Wool Museum","category":"museum","tags":["museums"],"location":{"lat":-38.14537,"lng":144.36122},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"geelong_national_wool_museum","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.nwm.vic.gov.au","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":4,"wikiPageviews":54,"wikidataSitelink